# PROPOSAL PATCH — build_variants.py env-gated NB (no-bind) variant.
# DO NOT APPLY while agent EM is live-editing the tree; apply together with
# 01-no-tostring-bind-guard.patch AFTER EM lands.
#
# Base state authored against: build_variants.py sha256 549b54dd... (EE
# state; NEXT-BUILD.md documents this as the current driver). Line numbers
# from that state; hunks are context-anchored.
#
# Design decisions (rationale in agent-EO-parallel-candidate.md):
# 1. ENV-GATED (L26_BUILD_NB=1): the standard A/B pipeline for EM's fixed
#    build keeps its exact current shape and build weight; the NB control
#    is an opt-in third twin-variant pair.
# 2. NB is A-SHAPED: it carries BOTH -DMODBRIDGE_L25_ENGINE_ADD_LISTENER
#    (CTOKEN, production registration) and -DMODBRIDGE_L27_NO_TOSTRING_BIND
#    (NBTOKEN, Phase 4c compiled out). 'define' becomes a list.
# 3. NB's define_units = NBTOKEN units UNION CTOKEN units, because the
#    single-define mechanism keys units off ONE token; without the union
#    UObjectArray.cpp would miss the CTOKEN define and compile the
#    KNOWN-BROKEN hand-rolled registration (#else path) — NOT A-shaped.
# 4. G4-nbtoken-present hard-fails at --execute when the guard is absent
#    (a missing token would silently make NB == A — the same no-op refusal
#    the driver already enforces for TOKEN/CTOKEN).
# 5. G11/G12 control gates: NB runtime must differ from A; per-unit object
#    deltas NB-vs-A must be EXACTLY ['unreal-unrealinitializer'] — the
#    scientific-control guarantee (single-delta vs variant A).
# 6. The A/B pair receipt (G9/G10) is untouched.

